# `s = """x "q" y"""` - single quotes inside a triple-quoted body.
#
# A reader that closes on any `"` stops at byte 9 and reads `q` as code. The
# literal runs [4, 17) off the source text, and `spans` is what states that -
# an earlier draft of this file wrote `lacks identifier` for the same idea and
# it was wrong in a way worth recording: `s` on the left of the assignment is
# an identifier too, so the claim could never hold no matter how the string
# parsed. A claim that cannot pass is exactly as useless as one that cannot
# fail, and this tier is supposed to catch both.
roots 1
mends 0
holds string_literal
spans string_literal 4 17
